Z||000000||Formula 18||09-07-2000||11:49 PM||||One--&gt; Will the rims from the new Grand Am fit on an 88? I likr the 16 inch rims with the 20 or so spokes and want a set from my ride.<P>Two--&gt; When I drive one the highway 70 or so I the front of the car seems to dance a little bit. It isn't a shimmy like bad balljoints. Aslo when I try and Park I can move the wheel likr an 1/10 of a turn before the wheel moves? I looked underneither and I don't think it is the tie rods. Bad rack maybe?? <P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000001||BroCar 87||09-08-2000||12:55 AM||||Formula 18: unless they have changed the bolt pattern and backspacing on those rims from earlier models, they SHOULD fit. The grand am is one of the other GM cars that have rims that fit the Fiero.<BR>Some other GM rims that fit are the Cavilier, Beretta, sunbird, and... I don't remember any others right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>About your 2nd question, sorry I have no answer for that one. I KNOW someone else on this forum knows though, these people are awesome with tech questions.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||09-08-2000||07:26 AM||||Gather you have an 88, if so check the pass side rack bushing for wear(look for up and down movement of the tie rod). Rodney has a $20 fix.||||reg||1
